{"title":"Welcome to Event Analytics Hub","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Welcome to Event Analytics Hub","description":"Introducing the platform — where written analysis meets interactive exploration.","author":"Dan Manastireanu","date":"2026-05-01","categories":["news","events"]},"headingText":"What is Event Analytics Hub?","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\nEvent Analytics Hub combines two things: written analysis and interactive\nexploration. Blog posts explain the concepts and show the key findings.\nDashboards let you dig into the data yourself.\n\n## How the blog and dashboards connect\n\nEvery analysis on this blog links to an interactive dashboard where you can\nexplore the data with your own filters. For example, here's a simple summary\nof event counts by quarter:\n\n```{r}\n#| label: quarterly-summary\n#| echo: true\n\nlibrary(ggplot2)\n\nevents <- data.frame(\n  period = c(\"Q1\", \"Q2\", \"Q3\", \"Q4\"),\n  count = c(120, 185, 210, 175)\n)\n\nggplot(events, aes(x = period, y = count, fill = period)) +\n  geom_col() +\n  labs(title = \"Event count by quarter\", x = \"Period\", y = \"Count\") +\n  theme_minimal() +\n  theme(legend.position = \"none\")\n```\n\nWant to filter this data by event type, source, or date range?\n\n[Explore this data in the dashboard →](http://localhost:3838/?period=Q3){.explore-cta}\n\n## What's next\n\nUpcoming posts will cover event models, stream processing patterns, and\ndashboard design with R Shiny and `bslib`.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## What is Event Analytics Hub?\n\nEvent Analytics Hub combines two things: written analysis and interactive\nexploration. Blog posts explain the concepts and show the key findings.\nDashboards let you dig into the data yourself.\n\n## How the blog and dashboards connect\n\nEvery analysis on this blog links to an interactive dashboard where you can\nexplore the data with your own filters. For example, here's a simple summary\nof event counts by quarter:\n\n```{r}\n#| label: quarterly-summary\n#| echo: true\n\nlibrary(ggplot2)\n\nevents <- data.frame(\n  period = c(\"Q1\", \"Q2\", \"Q3\", \"Q4\"),\n  count = c(120, 185, 210, 175)\n)\n\nggplot(events, aes(x = period, y = count, fill = period)) +\n  geom_col() +\n  labs(title = \"Event count by quarter\", x = \"Period\", y = \"Count\") +\n  theme_minimal() +\n  theme(legend.position = \"none\")\n```\n\nWant to filter this data by event type, source, or date range?\n\n[Explore this data in the dashboard →](http://localhost:3838/?period=Q3){.explore-cta}\n\n## What's next\n\nUpcoming posts will cover event models, stream processing patterns, and\ndashboard design with R Shiny and `bslib`.\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":false,"freeze":"auto","echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"knitr"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"show","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extensi